    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 31st March 2004, the matter described above is lawful within the meaning of section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reasons:\r\n\r\nThe rear extension, being 5.05m wide by 3.5m deep (with a step of 1.5m x 0.9m taken out of the south eastern corner), with a height of 2.8m, that adds a total of 46.11m3 to the volume of the original dwellinghouse, shown on the plans received on the 10th March 2004 constitutes permitted development as defined by Schedule 2, Part 1, Class A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 (as amended) and therefore does not require planning permission."
